<h2 id="how-to-create-click-to-whatsapp-ads-in-meta-ads-manager"><b>How to Create Click-to-WhatsApp Ads in Meta Ads Manager</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Creating a Click-to-WhatsApp Ad requires following simple steps. Once your Facebook Page and WhatsApp Business account are connected, you can create Click-to-WhatsApp ads in just a few minutes: </span></p>
<h3 id="step-1-open-meta-ads-manager"><b>Step 1: Open Meta Ads Manager</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Log in to Meta Ads Manager and tap the green </span><b>Create</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> button to begin a new campaign.</span></p>
<h3 id="step-2-choose-your-campaign-objective"><b>Step 2: Choose Your Campaign Objective</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Select between “</span><b>Engagement</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">” and “</span><b>Leads</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">” objectives that work best for your Click-to-WhatsApp campaign. Tap Continue.</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Lead: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">To generate inquiries and customer details </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Engagement: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">To increase WhatsApp conversations </span></li>
</ul>
<h3 id="step-3-select-your-messaging-destination"><b>Step 3: Select Your Messaging Destination</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Go to the Ad Set level and select </span><b>Messaging Apps </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">as your conversion location. Now choose </span><b>WhatsApp. </b></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">This tells Meta to send people directly to a WhatsApp conversation instead of a landing page.</span></p>
<h3 id="step-4-connect-your-number"><b>Step 4: Connect Your Number</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Now select your linked Facebook Page and choose your WhatsApp number from the drop-down menu, or click Connect another number.</span></p>
<p><b>Note: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Businesses running high-volume Click-to-WhatsApp campaigns often use the WhatsApp Business API to automate responses and manage leads more efficiently. If you’re not sure which platform to choose, explore our comparison of the </span><a href="/resources/blog/whatsapp-api-providers/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">best WhatsApp API providers</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. </span></p>
<h3 id="step-5-define-your-audience"><b>Step 5: Define Your Audience </b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Target the right people based on location, age, gender, interests, behaviours, custom audiences, and lookalike audiences. </span></p>
<h3 id="step-6-set-your-budget-and-schedule"><b>Step 6: Set Your Budget and Schedule</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Define your daily or lifetime budget and decide when your ads should start and stop. </span></p>
<h3 id="step-7-create-your-ad"><b>Step 7: Create Your Ad</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Upload your image, video, or carousel with a strong Call-to-action button like Send Message, Chat on WhatsApp, or Message Us. </span></p>
<h3 id="step-8-add-a-welcome-message"><b>Step 8: Add a Welcome Message</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">It’s time to add a pre-filled message that will appear the moment users enter the chat window as a warm welcome.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">You can also set up an automated greeting or automated replies to answer queries instantly, even outside business hours, with tools like </span><a href="/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Getgab’s AI Chatbot</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. </span></p>
<h3 id="step-8-review-and-publish"><b>Step 8: Review and Publish</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Double-check your campaign settings, targeted audience, message destination, and placements. Once everything looks right, tap Publish to launch your click-to-chat ad.</span></p>
<p><b>Tip:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Don’t stop after getting a click. Combine Click-to-WhatsApp Ads with </span><a href="/resources/blog/whatsapp-api-automation/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">WhatsApp API automation</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">, chatbots, and follow-up campaigns to turn more conversations into customers.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">If you’re new to Meta advertising, you can also check out our detailed guide on </span><a href="/resources/blog/whatsapp-ads/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">WhatsApp ads</span></a> <span style="font-weight: 400;">to learn about different ad formats and use them to generate leads and sales.</span></p>
<h2 id="what-happens-after-someone-clicks-understanding-whatsapp-s-free-messaging-window"><b>What Happens After Someone Clicks? Understanding WhatsApp’s Free Messaging Window  </b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Getting the click is just the beginning. Here’s what happens after someone taps your ads:</span></p>
<p><b>The 72-hour free window: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">When someone clicks your Click-to-WhatsApp Ad and sends a message, Meta opens a free 72-hour window. It means your business can reply within this window without any extra cost for message delivery.</span></p>
<p><b>The 24-hour customer service window: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Once the chat starts, a second timer begins. It is called the 24-hour customer service window that resets each time the customer sends a new message. In this window, your team and chatbot can send free-form replies.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Until now, these replies cost nothing. That’s about to change.</span></p>
<h3 id="what-changes-on-october-1-2026"><b>What Changes on October 1, 2026</b></h3>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">According to </span><a href="https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/business-messaging/whatsapp/pricing/non-template-messages" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Meta’s own developer documentation</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">, Meta will start charging for service messages sent inside the 24-hour window from October 1, 2026.  Here’s what you need to know:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Service messages get billed per message at the same rate as utility and authentication templates for each market. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Utility messages sent inside the window also lose their free status. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">It only affects the Meta WhatsApp API, not the free WhatsApp Business App. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">The good news is the 72-hour free window on Click-to-WhatsApp ads remains the same. Message delivery within this window remains free. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Meta plans to publish the exact rate by country on September 1, 2024. So check out your market’s current rate before getting started.</span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Each message reply inside the 24-hour window will carry a cost. This is where automation helps you out. With AI-based WhatsApp automation tools like HelloBotz, you can qualify leads faster and cut down on back-and-forth messages. </span></p>
<h2 id="common-click-to-whatsapp-ad-errors-and-how-to-fix-them"><b>Common Click-to-WhatsApp Ad Errors and How to Fix Them</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Even after setting up everything correctly, a few common issues can stop your CTWA before they go live. Here are common errors and their fixes: </span></p>
<h3 id="1-whatsapp-number-not-showing-up-in-the-dropdown"><b>1. WhatsApp Number Not Showing Up in the Dropdown</b></h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Why it happens:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Maybe because your Facebook Page is not linked to your WhatsApp Business account. </span></li>
<li><b>How to fix: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Go to your page settings and check your WhatsApp connection in your linked accounts. Try reconnecting if needed. </span></li>
</ul>
<h3 id="2-ad-gets-rejected"><b>2. Ad Gets Rejected</b></h3>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Why it happens: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Unclear creative, missing business details, or policy violation. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>How to fix:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> Review your ad copy and images. Ensure it matches Meta’s advertising policies and then resubmit. </span></li>
</ul>
<h3 id="3-welcome-message-or-automated-reply-not-sending"><b>3. Welcome Message or Automated Reply Not Sending</b></h3>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Why it happens: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Message templates require Meta’s approval before they can trigger. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>How to fix it</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">: Ensure your template is approved, enable the automation flow, and test the message before launching your campaign.</span></li>
</ul>
<h3 id="4-poor-ad-engagement-or-irrelevant-chats"><b>4. Poor Ad Engagement or Irrelevant Chats</b></h3>
<ul>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>Why it happens: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">Your ad promise does not match the WhatsApp conversation, or maybe users are not sure about what happens next after tapping. </span></li>
<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><b>How to fix</b><span style="font-weight: 400;">: Make sure your ad copy, creative, and welcome message deliver the same message or offer. Ask qualifying questions early and keep the conversation relevant. </span></li>
</ul>
